  m_text: 'A "fork bomb" is a malicious program that exhausts the system''s resources
    by spawning new processes, in an exponential matter. This overwhelms the system,
    at first making it slow, then making it unresponsive with the inevitable freezing
    of the system.


    These kinds of attacks can happen when the attacked platform
    will execute the binary, but only unhardened systems will actually crash, since
    most binaries are run in a sandbox.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
